    "why": "A SECOND PLANT THAT STAYED GREEN. Moving both filters from the window's START to its END changed nothing anywhere in the corpus, because no count case held a person whose level moved inside the window — and a window-located type has to choose a date, where a placement-located one simply uses the duty's. Owner decision M fixes it at the PERIOD START for target_per_period and this type follows, so the answer cannot depend on which date an implementation happened to ask about. p-ali is an R1 at the start of the week and an R2 by the end; p-noor is the mirror. The rule names R1, both hold three duties against a cap of two, and exactly one of them is flagged under each reading — so either direction of the mistake turns one row into the other.",
